        <h1 class="profile-detail-name">Addis Ababa</h1>
        <div class="info-stats" style="margin-top:10px;">
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Period</span><span class="info-stat-val">1886 CE – present</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Founded</span><span class="info-stat-val">Settlement began in 1886 at Finfinne, a place of hot springs; the site was chosen by Empress Taytu Betul, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/menelik-ii">Menelik II</a>, Negus of Shewa, moved his court there. The city became the capital of the empire in 1889.</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Where</span><span class="info-stat-val">In the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ethiopian-highlands">Ethiopian Highlands</a> at an elevation of 2,355 metres, at the foot of Mount Entoto and on the western edge of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-african-rift">Great Rift Valley</a>, in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ethiopia">Ethiopia</a> and surrounded by the Special Zone of Oromia.</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Known for</span><span class="info-stat-val">Taytu's house by the hot springs; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/menelik-ii">Menelik II</a>'s capital; the Italian occupation of 1936 to 1941; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/haile-selassie">Haile Selassie</a>'s return in 1941; the headquarters of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/organisation-of-african-unity">Organisation of African Unity</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/african-union">African Union</a>; the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-nations">United Nations</a> Economic Commission for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/africa">Africa</a>; the Merkato market</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Today</span><span class="info-stat-val">Addis Ababa is the capital and largest city of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ethiopia">Ethiopia</a>, a federally chartered city with an estimated 6.3 million inhabitants.</span></div>
